    {
      "flag": "declared-loss:uml.field-name-normalisation",
      "reason": "soundness-loss (complete-but-not-sound): FieldDef.name must match ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$ (src/core/models/meta.ts), so every camelCase UML property is snake_cased and xmi:id / xmi:type become xmi_id / xmi_type. The mapping is mechanical and reversible; an XMI importer must apply the inverse.",
      "state": "behind-flag"
    },
    {
      "flag": "declared-loss:uml.value-specification",
      "reason": "completeness-loss (sound-but-not-complete): The source schemas model defaultValue / specification / lowerValue / upperValue as z.lazy(() => z.any()), which the bridge rejects. They are modelled here as a closed ValueSpecification struct (UML 2.5.1 §8.3) limited to the literal arms plus opaque_expression; Expression trees with operands are not representable.",
      "state": "behind-flag"
    },
    {
      "flag": "declared-loss:uml.unlimited-natural",
      "reason": "soundness-loss (complete-but-not-sound): UnlimitedNatural (number | \"*\") is a field-level union, which the bridge stores as an opaque json-union string the host's kind check rejects. `upper` is an integer with -1 meaning unlimited; a consumer printing UML notation must map -1 back to '*'.",
      "state": "behind-flag"
    },
    {
      "flag": "declared-loss:uml.generalization-identity",
      "reason": "completeness-loss (sound-but-not-complete): Generalization, InterfaceRealization and Dependency are Elements with their own xmi:id in UML. They are modelled as relations (uml:Specializes, uml:Realizes, uml:DependsOn) carrying their attributes, so the relationship element's own identity and its comments are not preserved.",
      "state": "behind-flag"
    },
    {
      "flag": "declared-loss:uml.derived-unions",
      "reason": "completeness-loss (sound-but-not-complete): UML's derived unions (Namespace::member, Classifier::inheritedMember / feature / attribute, Namespace::importedMember) are not stored. They are derivable by traversing uml:Owns / uml:OwnsAttribute / uml:Specializes, and storing them would duplicate truth the host cannot keep consistent.",
      "state": "behind-flag"
    },
    {
      "flag": "declared-loss:uml.subset-scope",
      "reason": "completeness-loss (sound-but-not-complete): This profile realises the Foundation packages (CommonStructure, Classification, SimpleClassifiers, StructuredClassifiers, Packages). StateMachines, Activities, Interactions, UseCases, Components, Deployments and Profiles/Stereotypes are out of scope; the source library carries 110 metaclasses in total.",
      "state": "behind-flag"
    }
  ],
